# stack.branches: source of truth for this fork's PR branches and the combined main.
#
# Two concerns are kept separate on purpose:
#
#   * Each PR branch declares the base it rebases onto, 'base' (upstream, the
#     PR target) or another branch (a real dependency chain). This keeps every
#     branch's PR diff limited to its own work: independent fixes sit on 'base'
#     and never drag each other in.
#
#   * 'assemble' lists the order in which every branch's OWN commits are stacked
#     into the combined 'main' we run. main is a throwaway assembly of
#     cherry-picked copies, never a PR branch.
#
# Keywords:
#   base     <ref>               upstream ref; the PR target and default base.
#   into     <name>              the branch the assembly is written to.
#   branch   <name> onto <ref>   a PR branch; <ref> is 'base' or another branch.
#                                List a parent before any branch that sits on it.
#   assemble <name> ...          build order for the combined branch.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

base upstream/dev
into main
# -- 2026-11-10: upstream dev v1.11.0 (4bc53c6) took most of our features -------------
# komikndr reimplemented these in his own design rather than merging the branch tips
# (9f820c3 "Changing contract for config raylight, + ksanislo feature integrations"),
# so they are out of the build and their branches are kept only for reference:
#   feat/minimax-h3-fp16, feat/minimax-h3-fp16-node-inputs, feat/mlp-chunk  -> RayWorkerMinimaxOptions
#   feat/numa-aware-worker-placement, feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow,
#   feat/collective-timeout-option                     -> RayInitializerAdvanced inputs
#   feat/ray-kill-init, feat/minimax-h3-fun-controlnet (incl. the full-sequence fix)
#   feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode, feat/decode-cancel-and-progress -> his temporal decode
#   fix/worker-reset-cast-buffers' pin-eviction stubs  -> FSDPModelPatcher is no longer dynamic
# The config is immutable and node-driven now: the RAYLIGHT_* environment knobs the
# old branches read (ATTN_FP16, MLP_FP16, FP32_RESIDUAL, MLP_CHUNK_TOKENS, NUMA_BIND,
# PARALLEL_QUANT_LOAD, PG_TIMEOUT_MINUTES, WORKER_PIN, LORA_BYPASS) are not read.
# Out of the build for other reasons:
#   feat/initializer-input-ux - regrouped the old input order; upstream fixed a new one.
#   feat/fsdp-vae-decode, feat/single-vae-loader, feat/ray-audio-decode,
#   feat/vae-decode-row-split - their content is ported, minus the decoder sharding (off
#   in every workflow, no speedup), onto feat/decode-extras-on-native-temporal.
#
# Old tips of every branch rebuilt here are tagged pre-v111/<branch>.

# Comfy Kitchen INT8 as a Raylight inner-attention processor, ring support included:
# upstream's COMFY_KITCHEN_INT8 backend refuses ring_degree > 1 (no LSE). Needs our
# comfy-kitchen +lse build for int8_attention_with_lse.
branch feat/ck-int8-attention                 onto base
# Workers run outside ComfyUI's inference_mode; upstream's decode paths build an
# autograd graph (14.1 vs 5.1 GiB on a 43-frame decode). Upstream-able alone.
branch fix/vae-decode-no-grad                 onto base
# Ray 2.58 reads method options from the unwrapped function: upstream's
# @ray.method(num_returns=2) above @patch_ray_tqdm returns ONE ref, and every
# distributed decode dies in zip(*futures). Upstream bug, upstream-able alone.
branch fix/ray-method-under-wrapper           onto base
# 4bc53c6 gathers full K/V and runs dense attention whenever the sequence does not
# divide by the SP world size - nearly always - so ring and ck INT8 never ran
# (sampler 245 s vs 117 s) and every rank held the clip's whole K/V.
branch fix/minimax-usp-uneven-sequence-stays-distributed onto base
# On upstream's temporal decode: the VAE kept resident where the card can spare it,
# short clips and stills split across ranks by rows of tiles, Load VAE (Ray)'s host
# VAE output, VAE Decode Audio (Ray).
branch feat/decode-extras-on-native-temporal  onto fix/vae-decode-no-grad
# LoRA bypass deltas added in place, 8192 rows at a time (a 30 s 768p clip needs it),
# and the opt-in operand placement, which upstream's config no longer exposes.
branch feat/lora-bypass-memory                onto base
# The 32B prompt encoder sharded across the workers (RayCLIPLoader), its offload while
# sampling, cancel and progress.
branch feat/fsdp-text-encoder                 onto base
# Our wrapper around reset_cast_buffers: ComfyUI's reads dynamic_pins of every loaded
# dynamic model, which a pinless one would fail.
branch fix/worker-reset-cast-buffers          onto feat/fsdp-text-encoder
branch fix/offload-dit-while-encoding         onto feat/fsdp-text-encoder
# pin_ranks_to_gpus, appended last to RayInitializerAdvanced's inputs.
branch feat/rank-gpu-pinning                  onto base
branch tooling/stack                          onto base

assemble tooling/stack fix/ray-method-under-wrapper fix/minimax-usp-uneven-sequence-stays-distributed feat/ck-int8-attention fix/vae-decode-no-grad feat/lora-bypass-memory feat/fsdp-text-encoder fix/worker-reset-cast-buffers fix/offload-dit-while-encoding feat/decode-extras-on-native-temporal feat/rank-gpu-pinning
